Types of Operating Systems — With Real-Time Examples
Type of OS	Simple Meaning	Real-Time Example
1. Batch Operating System	Executes jobs in groups without continuous user interaction.	

Payroll processing — thousands of employee salaries are processed together.
2. Time-Sharing Operating System	Shares CPU time among multiple users/programs.

College computer lab — many students use the same server at the same time.

3. Multiprogramming OS	Keeps multiple programs in memory and switches between them to keep the CPU busy.	

Running a browser while a file is being downloaded.
4. Multitasking OS	Allows multiple tasks to run seemingly at the same time.	

Windows — listening to music while using Chrome and Word.

5. Multiprocessing OS	Uses multiple CPU cores/processors to execute tasks simultaneously.	

Modern laptop — different CPU cores handle Chrome, video playback, and other tasks.

6. Real-Time OS (RTOS)	Responds to events within a strict time limit.

Car airbag system — detects a crash and deploys the airbag immediately.
7. Distributed OS	Makes multiple connected computers work together as one system.

Distributed computing system — several computers cooperate to process a large task.

8. Network OS	Manages computers and resources connected through a network.	

Company network — employees access shared files and printers from a server.

9. Mobile Operating System	Designed for smartphones and tablets.	

Android — used on smartphones for apps, calls, camera, etc.

10. Embedded Operating System	Designed for a specific device or dedicated function.

Washing machine — controls washing, rinsing, spinning, and timing.
